Research Assistant in Social Network Data Analysis
Edinburgh - Easter Bush Campus, Midlothian, United Kingdom

Grade UE06: £35,302 - £40,704 per annum pro rata

CMVM / Royal (Dick) School of Veterinary Studies / Division of Global Agriculture and Food Systems

Part Time: 17.5 hours per week (2.5 days per week)

Fixed term: for 12 months

The Opportunity:

This role with contribute towards a greater understanding of the networked flow of climate information among pastoralists in Northern Kenya and Ethiopia using social network analysis. The objective of the project is to better understand the users of climate information forecasts and the flow of climate information at the local scale with the intention of better designing climate information technologies. In this role, the research assistant will carry out desk-based research of social network data gathered in Northern Kenya and Southern Ethiopia using social network analysis in R and/or Python. The post-holder will organise and map social network data to identify positions and role, hierarchies and cohesion, and the flow of information to different actors within the networks. This project is highly collaborative, and the research assistant will work with researchers and partners including the Alliance Biodiversity CIAT and University of Nairobi.

